WEBVTT

00:35.058 --> 00:36.692
Peter, what are you doing?

00:36.726 --> 00:38.327
I'm watching this
awesome show, Brian.

00:38.361 --> 00:40.495
See, they took all these colors
and they're making 'em

00:40.530 --> 00:42.197
all live together
in a beach house.

00:42.231 --> 00:44.733
Now the red one is sleeping
with the green one.

00:44.767 --> 00:47.269
And the blue one thinks he's
gonna have a career in music.

00:47.303 --> 00:49.271
And the yellow one
is just a total bitch.

00:49.305 --> 00:51.807
Peter, that's just a channel
that's gone off the air.

00:51.841 --> 00:53.275
<i>And we'll be right back with</i>

00:53.309 --> 00:56.745
<i>more Color Bar Beach House
after these messages.</i>

00:57.614 --> 00:58.880
Peter, for God's sake,

00:58.915 --> 01:01.116
did you eat this entire
roll of raw cookie dough?

01:01.150 --> 01:02.284
Oh, is that what that was?

01:02.318 --> 01:03.986
I thought it was
a raisin sausage.

01:04.020 --> 01:05.654
Peter, you're gonna get sick.

01:05.688 --> 01:07.889
You can't just eat raw food
out of the fridge.

01:07.924 --> 01:10.192
Eh, calm down,
people make mistakes.

01:10.226 --> 01:13.228
Just look at the original design
for the first hybrid car.

01:13.262 --> 01:15.397
Eric, we love the car.

01:15.431 --> 01:17.265
<i>We only want to
change one thing.</i>

01:17.300 --> 01:18.634
Is it the "rapist" sign?

01:18.668 --> 01:20.202
Yes, it is the "rapist" sign.

01:20.236 --> 01:21.403
I quit.

01:24.440 --> 01:27.242
So, as you can see,
our quarterly output is up

01:27.276 --> 01:28.677
one and a half percent.

01:28.711 --> 01:31.179
That's not net,
I'm talking gross.

01:31.214 --> 01:34.016
You do everything gross.

01:36.219 --> 01:40.022
<i>Stupid boring meeting.
I don't even want to be here.</i>

01:40.056 --> 01:43.291
<i>I'd rather be home, doing
dramatic garage door reveals.</i>

02:02.311 --> 02:04.946
And that gets us through
all projections...

02:06.315 --> 02:07.115
<i>What was that?</i>

02:08.518 --> 02:10.252
<i>Ah, that doesn't feel right.</i>

02:10.286 --> 02:12.954
<i>Ah, man, I think that cookie
dough is fighting that taco</i>

02:12.989 --> 02:14.656
<i>I found in the parking lot.</i>

02:14.691 --> 02:17.159
<i>I just hope I can hold it in
until the meeting's over.</i>

02:17.193 --> 02:21.163
And now, 23 minutes of silence
for the 23 workers

02:21.197 --> 02:23.832
who drowned in
the vats this year.

02:25.101 --> 02:26.735
Oh, God, it hurts.

02:26.769 --> 02:27.569
It hurts.

02:27.603 --> 02:29.071
Of course it hurts, Griffin.

02:29.105 --> 02:31.239
They were good men,
all of them.

02:31.274 --> 02:32.407
I can't hold it in!

02:32.442 --> 02:34.309
You don't have to, Griffin!

02:34.343 --> 02:35.377
Let it out!

02:35.411 --> 02:37.145
That's what we're here for.

02:37.180 --> 02:39.381
This was supposed to be
23 minutes of silence

02:39.415 --> 02:41.483
and there's kind of a lot of
conversation going on.

02:43.019 --> 02:45.520
Hey, Peter, my kid's selling
Girl Scout cookies and--

02:45.555 --> 02:47.289
We're collecting for
Janet's pregnancy--

02:47.323 --> 02:49.391
Softball sign-up--

02:49.425 --> 02:50.625
Trick or treat for UNICEF--

02:50.660 --> 02:52.194
Pitch in for Ed's
retirement cake?

02:52.228 --> 02:53.462
Holiday party?

02:53.496 --> 02:54.663
Whoa...!

02:54.697 --> 02:55.657
Company picnic--

02:55.665 --> 02:56.631
Secret Santa--

02:56.666 --> 02:57.432
Carpool info--

02:58.901 --> 03:01.069
Ah, finally, now I can
get myself to the--

03:10.580 --> 03:13.515
Ah, man, now everyone's gonna
remember me for this.

03:13.549 --> 03:16.051
I wanted to be remembered
for my achievement in film.

03:41.944 --> 03:43.478
There he is.

03:43.513 --> 03:44.980
Oh, oh, I see!

03:45.014 --> 03:46.748
Oh, you're all here
because you heard the news!

03:46.783 --> 03:47.916
Well, fine.

03:47.950 --> 03:50.218
Peter Griffin crapped himself
at work. Happy?

03:50.253 --> 03:50.897
Peter...

03:50.922 --> 03:52.721
No, no, Lois,
l-l-let's get it all out.

03:52.722 --> 03:55.157
<i>I'm sure you also heard that
someone walked into my office</i>

03:55.191 --> 03:56.625
while I was sucking
on my own toes.

03:56.659 --> 03:59.027
And do I go fast-walking
in nurse's shoes

03:59.061 --> 03:59.861
every Saturday in the park?

03:59.896 --> 04:01.096
Yes, I do.

04:01.130 --> 04:03.331
Peter, we're not here
because of any of that.

04:03.366 --> 04:05.400
Okay, I know what
this is about.

04:05.434 --> 04:06.995
Somebody saw me
holding hands with a guy

04:07.003 --> 04:08.336
at Quiznos this morning.

04:08.371 --> 04:10.872
All right, and was I involved in
the Oklahoma City bombing?

04:10.907 --> 04:11.940
A little bit.

04:11.974 --> 04:13.108
No, Peter,
you're not getting it.

04:13.142 --> 04:14.810
Okay, we'll go deeper.

04:14.844 --> 04:17.612
Yeah, I was swindled by that cat
who said he was from the future.

04:17.647 --> 04:19.381
Turns out he was
just a present-day cat

04:19.415 --> 04:20.682
with a smooth sales pitch.

04:20.716 --> 04:22.017
Dad, you don't understand.

04:22.051 --> 04:23.251
Oh, I understand.

04:23.286 --> 04:25.654
I understand I've made
hundreds of deadly enemies

04:25.688 --> 04:28.156
by shouting racial taunts
up at the jailhouse windows.

04:28.191 --> 04:29.224
Oh, and another thing,

04:29.258 --> 04:31.259
raise your hand if you
think ducks are magic.

04:31.294 --> 04:32.627
And... up it goes...!

04:32.662 --> 04:33.829
Peter's the only one.

04:33.863 --> 04:35.764
Peter, that's not
why they're here.

04:35.798 --> 04:39.134
A-And no, none of us heard about
you soiling yourself at work.

04:39.168 --> 04:40.235
Oh...

04:40.269 --> 04:41.603
well why is everybody here?

04:41.637 --> 04:43.939
Peter, your mother is dead.

04:43.973 --> 04:46.942
She had a stroke this
afternoon and she died.

04:46.976 --> 04:48.410
You don't die from that, Lois.

04:48.444 --> 04:50.512
You just host New Year's Eve
and talk funny.

04:50.546 --> 04:51.980
Peter, it's true.

04:52.014 --> 04:53.949
I'm so sorry.

04:53.983 --> 04:56.318
Oh, my God...

04:56.352 --> 04:58.620
I don't believe it.

04:58.654 --> 05:00.989
She's gone?

05:01.023 --> 05:03.959
All right, well, I'm gonna go
confuse everyone on Facebook

05:03.993 --> 05:07.562
with a, "So sad, terrible day"
status and nothing more.

05:33.618 --> 05:36.219
Your mother was
a good woman, Peter.

05:36.254 --> 05:37.554
Thanks, Lois.

05:37.588 --> 05:40.724
I just, I just can't believe
she's really gone.

05:40.758 --> 05:43.059
And I can't believe this
funeral home has a skylight

05:43.094 --> 05:45.495
with a sinister clown
staring down at us.

05:47.865 --> 05:49.699
Thank you for coming, everyone.

05:49.734 --> 05:52.736
We're here to celebrate
the life of Thelma Griffin.

05:52.770 --> 05:55.972
Here to say a few words
about Thelma is her son, Peter.

05:58.009 --> 05:59.876
My mother always hoped
to be buried

05:59.911 --> 06:01.411
with her pet cat, Mittens,

06:01.445 --> 06:04.114
so I'd like to thank
the Quahog Veterinary Society

06:04.148 --> 06:06.016
for putting Mittens down
so quickly.

06:06.050 --> 06:08.785
Yeah, just-just go ahead
and toss it in there.

06:08.819 --> 06:10.954
P-Probably, probably just
stuff it in by the feet.

06:12.823 --> 06:15.959
Okay, I will now take
questions from the audience.

06:15.993 --> 06:18.862
No? None? They don't
have to be about my mom.

06:18.896 --> 06:21.564
<i>Is anyone else here watching
Revolution and wanting</i>

06:21.599 --> 06:23.366
to talk about it after this?

06:23.401 --> 06:24.567
No! No! No! No!

06:24.602 --> 06:25.936
I'm not caught up!
I'm not caught up!

06:25.970 --> 06:29.706
Lotta white socks with
dress shoes in this bitch.

06:29.740 --> 06:30.974
God, I hate funerals.

06:31.008 --> 06:32.108
Yeah, they're stupid.

06:32.143 --> 06:33.843
Thank God I'm not
going to die.

06:33.878 --> 06:35.278
What do you mean?
Of course you are.

06:35.313 --> 06:36.613
I'm not gonna die, Brian.

06:36.647 --> 06:38.081
I'm like Jim Belushi.

06:38.115 --> 06:40.483
I am worried about
my funny brother, though.

06:40.518 --> 06:42.018
Food fight!

06:43.654 --> 06:46.823
This is tragic, but will
also open a door for me.

06:46.857 --> 06:48.925
Stewie, everyone is
gonna die, at some point.

06:48.960 --> 06:49.826
Everyone.

06:49.860 --> 06:51.895
So like... even me?

06:51.929 --> 06:52.896
Yes, even you.

06:52.930 --> 06:54.631
You are going
to die someday, Stewie.

06:54.665 --> 06:57.734
Wow... I guess you learn
something new everyday.

06:57.768 --> 06:59.369
Like the Black Eyed Peas.

06:59.403 --> 07:01.104
Hey, what's that?

07:01.138 --> 07:02.639
This is a guitar.

07:09.113 --> 07:13.216
Oh, Peter, look,
your mom's old photo albums.

07:13.250 --> 07:15.852
Oh, look at your
little baby footprints.

07:15.886 --> 07:18.488
Yeah, my mom took my footprint
every single year.

07:21.759 --> 07:24.127
When I was eight,
I was a dragon.

07:27.131 --> 07:29.466
Oh, hello.
You must be Cocoon.

07:29.500 --> 07:32.135
We don't have any rocks to make
you stronger here, but welcome.

07:33.304 --> 07:34.604
You must be Peter.

07:34.638 --> 07:36.806
I'm Evelyn, a friend
of your mother's.

07:36.841 --> 07:38.174
Oh, oh, hi.

07:38.209 --> 07:39.175
This is my family.

07:39.210 --> 07:40.643
They're of no comfort.

07:40.678 --> 07:43.279
Oh... I know it's tough
what you're going through.

07:43.314 --> 07:47.183
You're where I was 17 years ago,
when I lost my husband, Walter.

07:47.218 --> 07:49.119
He died of pancreatic cancer.

07:49.153 --> 07:51.221
That sounds sad,
but I didn't know him.

07:51.255 --> 07:53.156
Man, I miss my mom so much.

07:53.190 --> 07:55.925
Well, I knew your mother
better than anyone.

07:55.960 --> 07:57.761
I could tell you stories...

07:57.795 --> 07:59.562
Well, that sounds nice.

07:59.597 --> 08:01.965
Peter, the two of you
should hang out together.

08:01.999 --> 08:03.733
I'd like that very much.

08:03.768 --> 08:06.903
Well, it's 4:00.
I'm off to bed.

08:06.937 --> 08:09.406
Wow, Peter, looks like
you made a new friend.

08:09.440 --> 08:11.574
Yeah... a-and maybe
she can be my new mom,

08:11.609 --> 08:13.476
you know, just like Greg
Evigan and Paul Reiser

08:13.511 --> 08:15.311
were briefly my two dads.

08:15.346 --> 08:16.880
I keep forgetting your names.

08:16.914 --> 08:20.250
Can you just be "Jew Dad"
and you'll be "Earring Dad?"

08:30.728 --> 08:33.196
Stewie, could you please
stop tossing and turning?

08:33.230 --> 08:34.264
It's hard enough
to sleep in here

08:34.298 --> 08:36.099
without my memory
foam pillow.

08:36.133 --> 08:38.635
Uh... don't tell me,
don't tell me...

08:38.669 --> 08:39.836
Brian!
Yep.

08:39.870 --> 08:41.171
Yeah...

08:41.205 --> 08:43.306
I can't go to sleep,
Brian-- I'm scared!

08:43.340 --> 08:44.107
Of what?

08:44.141 --> 08:45.175
Of death!

08:45.209 --> 08:46.509
Well, you're not alone.

08:46.544 --> 08:48.611
The world is full of people
who can't accept death.

08:48.646 --> 08:49.846
And they've all got
their own ideas

08:49.880 --> 08:51.181
of what happens when we die.

08:51.215 --> 08:52.248
Really? Like what?

08:52.283 --> 08:54.417
Tell me, are any of them
blindly reassuring?

08:54.452 --> 08:55.652
Look, it's late.

08:55.686 --> 08:57.087
We'll talk about it
first thing tomorrow.

08:57.121 --> 08:58.354
Geez, you know, I gotta say,

08:58.389 --> 09:00.723
it's weird to see you
so worked up about this.

09:00.758 --> 09:02.125
I mean, you're
not afraid of anything.

09:02.159 --> 09:03.560
Even that monster
in your closet.

09:03.594 --> 09:05.328
Ah, he's on his way
out of here.

09:05.362 --> 09:07.330
Ever since he violated
the section of his lease

09:07.364 --> 09:09.499
that doesn't
allow subletters.

09:09.533 --> 09:10.433
What are you talking about?

09:10.468 --> 09:12.068
I don't have
anyone else in here.

09:12.103 --> 09:14.504
Just tell him
the truth, Ethan.

09:16.540 --> 09:18.007
Thank you for doing this, Brian.

09:18.042 --> 09:19.109
No problem, Stewie.

09:19.143 --> 09:21.911
Our first stop today
is a Jewish synagogue.

09:21.946 --> 09:25.281
Wow, every brick in this place
is named after someone.

09:25.316 --> 09:27.050
Yeah, they do that
to honor their donors.

09:27.084 --> 09:30.086
So that side of the building
was donated by someone named,

09:30.121 --> 09:31.421
"Get Out of Our Town"?

09:31.455 --> 09:33.490
No, I-I-I think that was
the work of some

09:33.524 --> 09:34.757
shaved-headed gentleman,

09:34.792 --> 09:36.793
but, but we're here
to talk about Judaism.

09:36.827 --> 09:38.728
So, where do they think
they go when they die?

09:38.762 --> 09:40.396
Well, you should try
asking the rabbi.

09:40.431 --> 09:42.732
Although, I should warn you,
you might not get an answer.

09:42.766 --> 09:45.568
So, where do Jewish people
think they go when they die?

09:45.603 --> 09:47.303
Where do you think we go?

09:47.338 --> 09:49.072
Well, I don't know.
That's why I'm asking you.

09:49.106 --> 09:51.674
Why do you think you're
asking all these questions?

09:51.709 --> 09:53.776
I-I just, I just really
want to know what happens.

09:53.811 --> 09:56.713
Do you think that's
part of God's infinite plan?

09:56.747 --> 09:59.282
I think your whole religion
is a sham, just so you can get

09:59.316 --> 10:00.950
extra holidays off from work.

10:00.985 --> 10:02.485
Oop, gotta go.
It's Buchwuch.

10:08.592 --> 10:10.760
I say, this is quite impressive.

10:10.794 --> 10:12.962
Buddhism is an
Asian religion that also has

10:12.997 --> 10:15.165
a significant following
of annoying white people.

10:15.199 --> 10:15.752
Okay.

10:15.777 --> 10:17.700
See, these guys believe
that after you die,

10:17.701 --> 10:19.335
you're reincarnated
and you come back

10:19.370 --> 10:21.371
as a pig or a cow
or a rooster.

10:21.405 --> 10:22.739
Okay, okay, that's good.

10:22.773 --> 10:24.941
I already know what noises
to make if I'm one of those.

10:24.975 --> 10:27.055
But they also don't believe
in demonstrating emotions

10:27.077 --> 10:28.878
either way, so they're
the worst people

10:28.913 --> 10:30.446
to buy birthday gifts for.

10:30.481 --> 10:32.515
I know you've been having
trouble getting around,

10:32.550 --> 10:34.317
so I bought you a new Lexus.

10:34.351 --> 10:36.119
And I got you
this tie clip.

10:36.153 --> 10:38.621
Thank you both.
These are equal to me.

10:38.656 --> 10:41.224
Screw you!
You don't even own a tie!

10:45.863 --> 10:48.631
Now, the Catholics believe that
as long as you accept Jesus

10:48.666 --> 10:50.934
before you die, anyone
can get into Heaven.

10:50.968 --> 10:52.135
Really? Anyone?

10:56.040 --> 10:58.007
I accept Jesus
as my Lord and Savior!

10:59.944 --> 11:01.177
Yes!

11:05.282 --> 11:08.318
Peter, thank you so much for
your help in making this cake,

11:08.352 --> 11:09.986
but don't you think
it would be easier

11:10.020 --> 11:11.387
if you stood
on the floor?

11:11.422 --> 11:13.423
Yeah, but when I baked
with my mom,

11:13.457 --> 11:15.024
I always stood
on a chair.

11:15.059 --> 11:17.994
Another memory is my Uncle Roy
putting his thumb in me.

11:18.028 --> 11:20.697
Ah, the best memories
are family memories.

11:20.731 --> 11:23.199
Oh, hey, Evelyn,
I got a riddle for you:

11:23.234 --> 11:25.702
What newspaper
do cows read?

11:25.736 --> 11:27.637
<i>The Moo York Times.</i>

11:27.671 --> 11:30.006
That's very clever, Peter.
Did you make that up?

11:30.040 --> 11:31.708
Nah, I got it off
a yogurt.

11:31.742 --> 11:33.209
Still, very impressive.

11:33.244 --> 11:34.510
God, you know, Evelyn,

11:34.545 --> 11:36.312
you've really helped me
through a tough time.

11:36.347 --> 11:38.181
I haven't been
this grateful

11:38.215 --> 11:40.049
since I met
the Sane Hatter.

11:40.084 --> 11:42.252
Excuse me. How do I get back
through the looking glass?

11:42.286 --> 11:43.586
Oh, yeah,
take two lefts

11:43.621 --> 11:45.488
and it's the first
door on your right.

11:45.522 --> 11:46.522
Cool. Great.

11:46.557 --> 11:48.091
Thanks for not giving me
the runaround.

11:48.125 --> 11:49.459
I-I asked that guy
over there,

11:49.493 --> 11:51.794
but he just told me
a bunch of rhyming nonsense.

11:51.829 --> 11:54.998
Oh, yeah-- he's, like,
a well-known dick.

12:00.504 --> 12:01.904
What are you
still doing awake?

12:01.939 --> 12:03.139
Changing the oil in my car!

12:03.173 --> 12:04.741
What the hell do you think
I'm doing?!

12:04.775 --> 12:07.577
Sorry, I stole that from the
Italian family next door.

12:07.611 --> 12:09.312
They've been going
at it all night.

12:09.346 --> 12:11.648
Dad, can I have five dollars
for lunch tomorrow?

12:11.682 --> 12:13.816
Yeah, sure, just
let me just go check

12:13.851 --> 12:15.518
my room full
of gold and jewels.

12:15.552 --> 12:18.955
You see, every first thing
he says is not the real thing.

12:18.989 --> 12:21.057
Anyway, Brian, I'm trying
to figure out death!

12:21.091 --> 12:23.326
It's not that
complicated, Stewie.

12:23.360 --> 12:25.528
Well, which of these religions
has the right answer?

12:25.562 --> 12:26.696
What-What about
you, Brian?

12:26.730 --> 12:28.665
What do you believe
happens when you die?

12:28.699 --> 12:30.667
Nothing.
Lights out. That's it.

12:30.701 --> 12:32.568
That's not comforting at all!

12:32.603 --> 12:34.370
Well, I just think
it's pretty clear

12:34.405 --> 12:36.572
that we're all just bags
of bones and flesh

12:36.607 --> 12:38.841
that eventually break down
and decay into worm food.

12:38.876 --> 12:41.177
We come from nothing,
and we're gonna become nothing.

12:41.211 --> 12:42.545
The end.
Night, Stewie.

12:44.114 --> 12:46.049
Lights out.

12:46.083 --> 12:48.017
Did you hear him, Rupert?

12:48.052 --> 12:50.019
Life is just a big joke.

12:50.054 --> 12:52.455
It's just sitting
around waiting to die.

12:52.489 --> 12:54.123
Well, I can't live like that.

12:54.158 --> 12:55.458
I'd rather just end it.

12:55.492 --> 12:57.093
I'm going to take my own life.

12:57.127 --> 12:59.696
But first, I'm gonna play ball
in the house.

13:00.764 --> 13:02.899
Parents are right!

13:05.969 --> 13:09.939
<i>We now return to
S.T., the Special Terrestrial.</i>

13:13.877 --> 13:15.978
Hi!

13:16.013 --> 13:17.347
Hey, guys,
this is Evelyn.

13:17.381 --> 13:19.048
She's the one
with that bathroom carpet

13:19.083 --> 13:21.184
I've been peeing on
I told you about.

13:21.218 --> 13:22.552
Hey, nice to meet you.

13:22.586 --> 13:24.721
You know, instead
of drawing on your eyebrows,

13:24.755 --> 13:26.522
maybe just go without
eyebrows.

13:26.557 --> 13:29.092
And I'm Joe Swanson.

13:29.126 --> 13:31.361
I've been dying to introduce
you guys to Evelyn.

13:31.395 --> 13:33.196
We've just been having
the best time together.

13:33.230 --> 13:34.630
Evelyn, tell them
how many sodas

13:34.665 --> 13:36.165
I combined at the movie theater.
Two.

13:36.200 --> 13:38.468
It was more than that.
She fell asleep.

13:38.502 --> 13:42.138
She let me drive
a little bit on the way home.

13:42.172 --> 13:43.539
Just in the parking lot.

13:43.574 --> 13:45.708
But you were a good
little navigator.

13:47.077 --> 13:50.380
Yeah, I just remembered, I gotta
get the hell out of here.

13:54.084 --> 13:56.619
Well, God said I could
walk just one time.

13:56.653 --> 13:59.789
I was saving it for
Susie's wedding day, but...

14:03.260 --> 14:04.761
Your friends seem lovely.

14:04.795 --> 14:06.095
Ah, they a'ight.

14:06.130 --> 14:09.132
You know, Evelyn, I am having
such a good time with you.

14:09.166 --> 14:10.967
You're like
my aboveground mom.

14:11.001 --> 14:13.236
Oh, Peter, you know, sometimes

14:13.270 --> 14:15.138
I think your mother
brought us together.

14:15.172 --> 14:16.806
Yeah, tha-that's how I feel.

14:16.840 --> 14:18.007
Good.

14:28.919 --> 14:31.988
Come on. Are you molesting me
or watching TV?

14:36.431 --> 14:39.132
I can't believe that
old woman kissed you!

14:39.167 --> 14:40.400
Oh, it was horrible, Lois.

14:40.435 --> 14:42.636
There were still crumbs
in the corners of her mouth

14:42.670 --> 14:45.339
from that Nilla Wafer
she had at lunch.

14:45.373 --> 14:47.574
Are you sure there wasn't
some kind of misunderstanding?

14:47.575 --> 14:49.343
No, no, those were
definitely Nilla Wafers.

14:49.377 --> 14:51.345
And it really
bums me out, you know,

14:51.379 --> 14:53.613
'cause I thought she was
something special.

14:53.648 --> 14:55.482
She was like a mom to me.

14:55.516 --> 14:57.718
Well, then you should
go talk to her

14:57.752 --> 14:59.286
and try to clear
this up.

14:59.320 --> 15:01.688
It sounds weird, but
maybe it was innocent.

15:01.723 --> 15:03.523
I mean, this wouldn't
be the first time

15:03.558 --> 15:05.258
you thought someone
was hitting on you.

15:05.293 --> 15:07.394
Would you like
to add chips and a drink?

15:07.428 --> 15:09.196
Here we go again.

15:14.068 --> 15:16.303
All right, Rupert, here we go.

15:20.375 --> 15:23.176
Well, I'm not dead,
but I do have a boner.

15:23.211 --> 15:26.346
So that is something new
about Stewie.

15:28.483 --> 15:31.084
Okay, death by cop.

15:33.388 --> 15:35.288
Hey, copper, come get me!

15:35.323 --> 15:37.257
Oh, no, an armed assailant!

15:37.291 --> 15:39.493
I definitely don't want
to die today.

15:39.527 --> 15:42.662
I have so much
to live for.

15:42.697 --> 15:44.131
Come on! Shoot me!

15:44.165 --> 15:46.967
The one day I don't wear
my bulletproof vest!

15:47.001 --> 15:49.102
What are you waiting for?
I'm wide open!

15:49.137 --> 15:51.638
Don't you hate how the heart
is right about here?

15:51.672 --> 15:54.040
Just kiss, you fruitcakes!

15:58.012 --> 16:01.047
All right, Rupert, the old
toaster in the tub never fails.

16:07.889 --> 16:10.991
Oh, damn, I wanted to die,
not turn into Toaster Man.

16:14.028 --> 16:15.662
I don't know
about this Toaster Man.

16:15.696 --> 16:18.331
While he's getting all the
glory, John Q. Taxpayer is left

16:18.366 --> 16:19.733
to clean up the crumbs.

16:21.169 --> 16:24.304
My breakfast bread
just got perfectly browned!

16:24.338 --> 16:26.473
I just wish I could thank him!

16:26.507 --> 16:28.141
Oh, I think he knows, Pop.

16:28.176 --> 16:30.577
I think he knows.

16:34.048 --> 16:36.249
Evelyn, we need to talk.

16:36.284 --> 16:38.985
Oh, Peter,
I owe you an apology.

16:39.020 --> 16:42.088
I'm afraid my new medicine
made me act foolishly yesterday.

16:42.123 --> 16:44.191
You must forgive me.
Oh.

16:44.225 --> 16:47.260
So it-it was, it was
just your medicine, huh?

16:47.295 --> 16:49.296
Well, I guess I can
understand that.

16:49.330 --> 16:51.131
You know, I'm addicted
to nasal spray.

16:52.934 --> 16:55.735
I smell everything!
I'm invincible!

16:59.540 --> 17:01.575
I'm probably gonna be
a little down

17:01.609 --> 17:03.577
until I use
the spray again.

17:03.611 --> 17:05.779
That's okay, Peter.
Now come along.

17:05.813 --> 17:08.748
I've got quite the day
planned for us.

17:09.784 --> 17:11.818
♪ She's just a devil woman

17:11.853 --> 17:13.753
♪ With evil on her mind

17:13.788 --> 17:16.156
♪ Beware the devil woman

17:16.190 --> 17:18.158
♪ She's gonna get you

17:18.192 --> 17:20.026
♪ She's just a devil woman

17:20.061 --> 17:22.262
♪ With evil on her mind

17:22.296 --> 17:23.763
♪ Beware the devil woman

17:23.798 --> 17:26.299
♪ She's gonna get you
from behind. ♪

17:35.209 --> 17:36.776
Evelyn, I think it's best

17:36.811 --> 17:38.678
that we don't see
each other anymore.

17:38.713 --> 17:39.779
But Peter...

17:39.814 --> 17:41.181
No, Evelyn, I trusted you,

17:41.215 --> 17:42.949
and all this funny business
keeps happening,

17:42.984 --> 17:44.918
and I don't think
it's your medicine at all.

17:44.952 --> 17:47.020
So I'm afraid this is good-bye.

17:47.054 --> 17:49.523
But Peter, I thought
we were friends.

17:49.557 --> 17:51.258
Yeah, right.
You tricked me!

17:51.292 --> 17:53.860
You're as bad as those
predators on the Internet.

17:53.895 --> 17:55.462
That's wild, Stacey.

17:55.496 --> 17:58.465
I'm a 12-year-old girl, too.

17:58.499 --> 18:00.567
My name's Jenny.

18:00.601 --> 18:04.104
Want to come over to my place
and help me move?

18:06.874 --> 18:08.675
Hey, you're not
a 12-year-old girl!

18:08.709 --> 18:10.777
Neither are you, Jenny!

18:10.811 --> 18:13.380
Huh. I guess we aren't
so different after all.

18:13.414 --> 18:15.549
Yeah. You know, this isn't
a whole lot of stuff.

18:15.583 --> 18:17.884
We can probably knock
this out in an hour.

18:26.294 --> 18:27.460
What the hell?!

18:28.563 --> 18:30.230
Stewie, what the hell
are you doing?!

18:30.264 --> 18:33.166
He's doing his taxes!
What's it look like he's doing?

18:33.200 --> 18:35.335
Vito, get away from
the neighbors' house!

18:35.369 --> 18:36.670
I'm killing myself,
Brian.

18:36.704 --> 18:38.338
You said it yourself,
when we die,

18:38.372 --> 18:40.507
there's nothing!
We just rot in the ground!

18:40.541 --> 18:41.775
Well, if life has
no purpose,

18:41.809 --> 18:43.410
why not just cut
to the chase?

18:43.444 --> 18:44.878
Look, Stewie, I know
you're worried,

18:44.912 --> 18:47.314
but you can't live your life
being scared of death.

18:47.348 --> 18:48.815
Nobody knows
what comes next,

18:48.849 --> 18:51.384
so all we can do is pack
the most we can

18:51.419 --> 18:52.752
into each day we've got.

18:52.787 --> 18:54.287
So for you,
that's taking

18:54.322 --> 18:56.790
a 45-minute shaky-leg poop
on the front lawn?

18:56.824 --> 18:57.991
I'm just saying
there's something

18:58.025 --> 18:59.826
to be said for living
in the moment.

18:59.860 --> 19:01.328
So what you're saying is

19:01.362 --> 19:03.229
<i>I've got to find
my shaky-leg poop.</i>

19:03.264 --> 19:05.031
Exactly.

19:05.066 --> 19:06.499
Well, I-I have
always wanted

19:06.534 --> 19:08.535
to be a singer-songwriter.

19:08.569 --> 19:11.071
Um... yeah. No, yeah,
you could do that.

19:11.105 --> 19:12.372
You-You paused.

19:12.406 --> 19:13.540
Why-Why did you pause?

19:13.574 --> 19:15.442
Uh... no reason.

19:15.476 --> 19:17.444
You did it again!
I swear to God,

19:17.478 --> 19:19.412
I will throw myself
right out that window!

19:19.447 --> 19:21.915
Okay, welcome
to the Apple Tree Pub.

19:21.949 --> 19:24.284
I'm Stewie Griffin,
and these...

19:24.318 --> 19:26.953
are my six assistants.

19:26.988 --> 19:28.321
You know,
I changed my mind.

19:28.356 --> 19:29.856
Kill yourself.

19:33.628 --> 19:36.663
Hey, Mom, I-I gotta talk
to you about something.

19:36.697 --> 19:38.798
You know, ever since
you turned into a rock

19:38.833 --> 19:40.133
with your name on it,

19:40.167 --> 19:43.169
your friend's been
really inappropriate with me.

19:43.204 --> 19:45.138
Hello, Peter.

19:45.172 --> 19:46.272
Oh. Hi.

19:46.307 --> 19:48.108
What are you doing here?

19:48.142 --> 19:49.976
Peter, I want
to apologize.

19:50.011 --> 19:52.445
<i>I did behave
inappropriately.</i>

19:52.480 --> 19:54.581
It's just that since my beloved
Walter died,

19:54.615 --> 19:57.617
you're the first man who's paid
any attention to me,

19:57.652 --> 20:00.654
and I guess I took advantage
of that.

20:02.156 --> 20:04.724
Well, you know, when-when
you put it that way,

20:04.759 --> 20:08.061
I guess maybe it's a little bit
my fault, too.

20:08.095 --> 20:10.163
I missed my mom so much,

20:10.197 --> 20:14.300
and I guess maybe I sort of
used you as a replacement.

20:14.335 --> 20:17.504
I'm glad we
became friends, Evelyn.

20:26.781 --> 20:29.382
Evelyn? Evelyn?!

20:46.517 --> 20:48.722
Looks like somebody's mom died
or something,

20:48.723 --> 20:51.276
I don't know. You--You'll take
care of this, right?

20:51.277 --> 21:52.277
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru